            <title><![CDATA[Blanche wins support from GOP holdouts after vowing to scrap 'anti-weaponization fund']]></title>
            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/blanche-wins-support-from-gop-holdouts-after-vowing-to-scrap-anti-weaponization-fund</link>
            <description><![CDATA[Acting Attorney General Todd Blanche cleared a major hurdle in his push to permanently lead the Department of Justice. He reached a deal with two GOP senators who had said they would block his nomination. Blanche put into writing that the DOJ is scrapping a $1.8 billion "anti-weaponization" fund that could have provided settlements to the Trump allies, including Jan. 6 rioters. Ali Rogin reports.]]></description>
